7924 0 obj
  << /ActualText (This project supports the integration of Indigenous perspectives within Durham College\031s Field\021to\021Fork\021to\021Field campus model and reflects our ongoing responsibility to engage in meaningful work toward Reconciliation\056 In partnership with the Barrett Centre of Innovation in Sustainable Urban Agriculture\054 students gain hands\055on experience in GHG\021reduction strategies through culinary programming\054 applied research\054 and industry\055informed workshops\056 \n\nIndigenous knowledge systems and voices are centred with the development of an Indigenous Healing Garden and integrated throughout learning\054 including garden design and creation in partnership with Miinikaan and a ground blessing ceremony led by Elder Dorothy Taylor\056 It invites our community to learn through relationships with the land and with the Indigenous knowledge systems and communities for sustainability\056 Community events and GHG\055conscious culinary workshops model sustainable food preparation\054 composting\054 and waste\021reduction practices\054 supported by biodigester and food\021 waste data shared through public outreach\056 )
     /K [ 5 ]
     /P 7925 0 R
     /Pg 4326 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

