7948 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Each year\054 the campus cafeteria generates a significant amount of food waste which\054 when sent to landfill\054 contributes to greenhouse gas emissions\056 Through\240ImpAct\240Climate\240microfunding\054 a dehydrator was\240acquired\240in 2024 to divert this waste from landfill\054 then grind and dry it\056\n\240\nThe main\240objective\240of this phase of the project is to reduce the campus carbon footprint by diverting food waste from\240landfill\054\240while enhancing its agronomic potential\056 More specifically\054 the project aims to test the effectiveness of the dry substrate produced by the dehydrator on the growth of Indigenous medicinal plants\054 cultivated in partnership with the First Nations\054\240M\351tis\240and Inuit Education Centre at Coll\350ge\240Bor\351al\056\240\n\nThe project also includes the organization of awareness workshops open to the community\054 in collaboration with the City of Greater Sudbury and the Junction Creek Stewardship Committee \050JCSC\051\056 These activities aim to promote waste sorting and the reduction of food waste\054 as well as to better understand the impact of waste on the local environment\056\240)
     /K [ 5 ]
     /P 7949 0 R
     /Pg 4934 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

