8068 0 obj
  << /ActualText (On October 28\054 2025\054 Conestoga College hosted a Micro\055Forest planting initiative as part of its broader climate action and campus rewilding efforts\056 The event engaged 40 students\054 faculty\054 and staff in a three\055hour hands\055on planting activity\054 resulting in the installation of over 100 native shrubs and trees\056\n\nBeyond increasing campus biodiversity\054 the initiative directly contributes to greenhouse gas \050GHG\051 reduction\056 Over their lifetime\054 the planted species are expected to sequester approximately 200\023250 kg of carbon annually \024 roughly equivalent to the annual energy use of one household\056 \n\nThe planting plan was informed by Indigenous knowledge and perspectives through consultation with Indigenous community leadership\056 This approach ensured that species selection and ecological planning reflected local land\055based knowledge systems and principles of environmental stewardship\056)
     /K [ 5 ]
     /P 8069 0 R
     /Pg 7654 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

